{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For HaShem your Elohim, He is the Elohim of elohim.</b> The angels. <b>And HaShem of lords,</b> the spheres, for they are lords over every body. <b>The El,</b> He is the Creator, and He is <b>the great,</b> in kindness, <b>the mighty,</b> in judgment, <b>and the awesome,</b> in mercy. And these are the totality of the supernal attributes called fathers, concerning which it is said: the fathers, they themselves are the chariot. And I have already mentioned in Ki Tissa that Moses our teacher, peace be upon him, included in these three praises the thirteen attributes that were spoken to him at Sinai." "<b>Who shows no partiality.</b> To the perfect righteous man, because of the abundance of his merits, that He would not punish him even for a light transgression." "<b>And takes no bribe.</b> A transgression in exchange for a commandment, for He does not say: since he performed a thousand commandments and committed one transgression, I will deduct one commandment from him on account of the transgression he committed, and the commandment will offset the transgression; rather, He punishes him for that single transgression and gives him reward for the multitude of commandments, all of them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :register {:fixes 1}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:15.567264592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}